intent:
  id: intent/2026-07-26/live-runner-pool-preflight
  change_type: feature
  scope: GitHub runner pool readiness validation
  summary: Fail before runner installation when the GitHub App cannot register organization runners or inspect configured Actions queues.
  decision: Add a read-only pool-check command that requests and discards a narrowly scoped runner registration token, then snapshots queue and runner state with a separately read-narrowed installation token.
  constraints:
    - Preflight tokens must be scoped to configured repositories and only the permissions required for each check.
    - Registration, installation, and API tokens must never be logged.
    - Permission and repository failures must provide actionable guidance without echoing GitHub response bodies.
    - The command must not create a runner or other GitHub resource.
    - Existing runtime registration behavior remains compatible.
  intent_priority: must
  code_locations:
    - Sources/sand/PoolCheck.swift
    - Sources/sand/GitHub/GitHubService.swift
    - Sources/sand/Sand.swift
    - Tests/sandTests/GitHubRunnerPoolMonitorTests.swift
    - Tests/sandTests/GitHubServiceTests.swift
